		},
		{
			"id":"27dd418f63edbb25",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"Dynamical Billiards",
			"type":"text",
			"x":390,
			"y":-2800,
			"width":250,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"df9729b1466796a6",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"text":"# Side Projects\n\n- [ ] solving an orbital mechanics problem numerically (gravitational force + radiation pressure force) and analyze using dynamical systems methods.\n- [ ] Evolving a distribution in phase space\n- [ ] solving the ray equation numerically\n- [ ] Real about [Capacitance & Grounding](Capacitance%20&%20Grounding.md)\n- [ ] Explore the propagation of pulses in dielectric media as opposed to metals.\n\t- [ ] Figure out the amplitude of an EMP pulse\n\t- [ ] understand, given the amplitude of a pulse, how thick would metal walls (Faraday cage) have to be in order to provide protection\n- [ ] A code that takes daily food intake in grams (over a week) and returns average daily distribution of food as well as weekly macronutrient distribution and micronutrient amounts relative to recommended daily amounts. Also - fat profile (omega3 to omega6 ratios, and types of fats consumed saturated, monounsaturated and polyunsaturated).\n- [ ] Error propagation for \"non-differentiable\" functions (e.g functions that are made in function).\n- [ ] **Dynamical Billiards** - implementation attempt using the ray equation and seeing if maybe a complex refractive index can mimic a metal and result in specular reflection.\n\n- [ ] 2D gas in discrete cells\n- [ ] OOP - make the particle an object?\n\t- [ ] each cell (state) can occupy one molecule at a time\n\t- [ ] time evolution\n\t- [ ] reaching equilibrium\n\t- [ ] assessing entropy\n\n- [ ] Modes of coupled oscillators can be excited given the right frequencies. In principle - the more DOFs such a system has the more available resonant frequencies for exciting the modes of the system. Does an infinite chain of coupled oscillators have infinite number of modes?\n- [ ] Physics of lightning bolts\n- [ ] [Ultra Violet Index](../../3.%20Problems/Ultra%20Violet%20Index.md)\n- [ ] Solving the wave equation numerically on a general boundary (perhaps created by Bezier curves).\n",
			"type":"text",
			"dynamicHeight":true,
